  <section id="trip-length">
    <p class="eyebrow">Reality Check</p>
    <h2>Compare the whole cost, not just the nights</h2>
    <p>Shorter stays reduce lodging and daily expenses, but airfare changes with the dates and routing. A seven-night trip is not automatically half the price of a twelve-night trip. Compare current quotes before choosing a length.</p>
    <div class="lm-grid">
      <div class="lm-card">
        <h3>Portugal: current full-trip estimate</h3>
        <p>{{ hub.portugal.pto.nights }} hotel nights for the family of four.</p>
        <p><strong>{{ hub.portugal.budget.floorUsd | money }}–{{ hub.portugal.budget.ceilUsd | money }} cash</strong></p>
        <p>These are itemized planning allowances, not a guaranteed booking price. The protected multi-city airfare and internal flights must be priced together.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="lm-card">
        <h3>Short escapes: separate comparison</h3>
        <p>The short-escape cards below use full cash budgets and a separate ranking.</p>
        <p>Compare the same travelers, baggage, room occupancy and included activities when weighing a short trip against a longer one.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="lm-card">
        <h3>Protect usable vacation time</h3>
        <p>Compare hotel nights, flight arrival times, base changes and recovery time—not just calendar days. Jet lag varies; a fixed number of “good days” is not promised.</p>
        <p>Shortening a trip may change airfare, PTO and the Nights score. No hypothetical shorter variant changes the canonical ranking. Every option must preserve the full June 24–26, 2027 Pittsburgh commitment.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
